ted the root with exact rational arithmetic, and rejected a planted sunflower, a planted containment and an inflated bound · Not peer reviewed ... Gluing copies of a 6,341-set Sperner, 3-sunflower-free family on 20 points (the chain construction of Lemma 4.4 of Deuber, Erdős, Gunderson, Kostochka and Meyer, 1997) gives μ_{3} ≥ ((3901 + √5882425)/2)^{1/18} = 1.5647730960…, against 1.551 in that paper and an unpublished 1.554. ... Earlier values: 1.5617847 (30 September 2026) and 1.5621220 (1 October 2026), whose certificates are in irsi-certificates-2026-10-01.zip (SHA-256 f89d9255e75860d4a9d08ab2b96ac8b891a02bf53340171c9320563a2afe3a6d, folder `sunflower`) with three exact checkers, one by Google Gemini, and an OpenAI GPT-6 recheck.\n## The 3-sunflower-free capacity is at least 1.5647730\n\nLast updated 2026-10-17\n\n17 October 2026 (earlier values 1.5617847 on 30 September and 1.5621220 on 1 October 2026) · Exact certificate, accepted by three exact checkers written separately. One was written from scratch by OpenAI GPT-6.1 Sol (a second model provider), given only the definitions and the 1997 paper: it checked all 20,100,970 containment pairs and 292,854,591 sunflower completions, re-derived the transfer matrix and the gluing lemma, isolated the root with exact rational arithmetic, and rejected a planted sunflower, a planted containment and an inflated bound · Not peer reviewed\n\nA family of subsets of an n-element set with no three members whose pairwise intersections are all equal has at most μ_{3}^{n+o(n)} members. Gluing copies of a 6,341-set Sperner, 3-sunflower-free family on 20 points (the chain construction of Lemma 4.4 of Deuber, Erdős, Gunderson, Kostochka and Meyer, 1997) gives μ_{3} ≥ ((3901 + √5882425)/2)^{1/18} = 1.5647730960…, against 1.551 in that paper and an unpublished 1.554.\n\nCheck it\n\nAspect5/sunflower-free-capacity, tag v1.2: certificate `cert_c49_chain20_v12.json` (SHA-256 7472112ced9d98da8cf7b6a3d586b93ea66750e39989e7a6d6d5f52ffeb4e82e