owth rate of $f(w,k)$.We also prove a general upper bound for $3$-uniform families with at least four petals.Our results give $39\\le f(3,4)\\le49$, $f(3,5)\\le146$, $153\\le f(3,6)\\le255$, $259\\le f(3,7)\\le474$, and $54\\le f(4,3)\\le83$.\nTitle: Sunflower-Free Uniform Families: Recursive Constructions and Explicit Bounds\nAuthors: Edward Axante, Cristian Budala, David Chitic, Bogdan Dumitru, Mihai Nacu\nDate: Sat Sep  5 16:31:55 2026\n\nLet $f(w,k)$ be the maximum size of a $w$-uniform family containing no sunflower with $k$ petals. We introduce a recursive construction for sunflower-free families and use it to obtain a general lower bound on the exponential growth rate of $f(w,k)$. We also prove a general upper bound for $3$-uniform families with at least four petals. Our results give $39\\le f(3,4)\\le49$, $f(3,5)\\le146$, $153\\le f(3,6)\\le255$, $259\\le f(3,7)\\le474$, and $54\\le f(4,3)\\le83$. In addition, we prove that the maximum size of an intersecting $4$-uniform family containing no sunflower with three petals is $27$. The upper bounds $49$ and $83$ are computer-assisted. The finite lower bounds come from explicit constructions.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVibeMathed - Math Problems Solved by AI (https://vibemathed.com/)\nciteturn155search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; (The manuscript claims a computer-assisted exclusion of 69-member three-sunflower-free four-uniform families, giving 54 <= M(4,3) <= 68. ... Axante, Budala, Chitic, Dumitru and Nacu (arXiv:2609.06175v1, September 2026, Table 1 and Theorem 6.9) improved the upper bound to 83, so $54\\le f(4,3)\\le83$54≤f(4,3)≤83.\n### Maximum size of a three-sunflower-free family of four-element sets\n\n0 0\n\nProved Partial AI-assisted\n\n(The manuscript claims a computer-assisted exclusion of 69-member three-sunflower-free four-uniform families, giving 54 <= M(4,3) <= 68. It improves the upper bound 83 in Axante et al., arXiv:2609.06175v1, Theorem 6.9. The classical lower construction is reproduced, not claimed as new. The proof combines their intersecting-family bound 27, structural point-link reductions, Jin's graph-homomorphism theorem, exact certificates and finite exhaustive checks. A local cap of 61 requires a complete R16 point-link and is not a global bound. Cardinality 68 is not excluded, the exact value is not determined, and the general sunflower conjecture (Erdős #20) remains open.)\n\nExtremal set theory; sunflowers and finite set systems\n\nHow large can a family of distinct four-element sets be if no three of its members form a sunflower, that is, three distinct members whose pairwise intersections are all equal (an empty common intersection included)? Write $f(4,3)$f(4,3) for this maximum.\nAbbott, Hanson and Sauer (1972) gave $f(4,3)\\le142$f(4,3)≤142 and Abbott and Hanson (1974) gave $f(4,3)\\ge54$f(4,3)≥54. Axante, Budala, Chitic, Dumitru and Nacu (arXiv:2609.06175v1, September 2026, Table 1 and Theorem 6.9) improved the upper bound to 83, so $54\\le f(4,3)\\le83$54≤f(4,3)≤83. The exact value is open. The forcing-threshold convention used for Erdős Problem #20 is one larger than $f(4,3)$f(4,3).\n\nPosed by Abbott, Hanson and Sauer (1972, upper bound 142) and Abbott and Hanson (1974, lower bound 54), as recorded in Axante et al., arXiv:2609.06175v1, Table 1·Open —[Button: *]·Model Sol 5.6; Astra 6; Pro 6; Sol 6.1 (OpenAI)·Solved 2026-10\n\nAnnounced Significance 9[Button: *]Submitted by Oleksiy Babanskyy on 9 Oct 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA1K Agentic SuperMath · Transversal Six, Finite Obstructions and Boundary Profiles in Rank-Four Sunflower-Free Families (https://a1k.ai/agentic-math/rank-four-sunflower-free-families)\nciteturn155search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; The inherited local formalization establishes unconditional ceilings G(93) and I(41), lower-bound witnesses with fifty-four unrestricted members a